  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/5a0f6d3e4c4a02aa50d37df9a85ad466f41404d2</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/jenkinsci/pipeline-input-step-plugin/commit/5a0f6d3e4c4a02aa50d37df9a85ad466f41404d2"/>
    <title>
        Fix X-Dialog-Title header mangling uppercase letters, digits and &#39;?&#39;
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:51:24Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21194782?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>timja</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/timja</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Fix X-Dialog-Title header mangling uppercase letters, digits and &amp;#39;?&amp;#39;

The regex in dialog.jelly reached java.util.regex with doubled backslashes,
so the character class contained the range &amp;#39;0-\&amp;#39; (0x30-0x5C) and replaced
digits, &amp;#39;?&amp;#39;, &amp;#39;@&amp;#39; and A-Z with spaces. A message starting or ending with one
of those produced a header value with leading or trailing whitespace, which
HTTP/2 rejects, so the dialog fetch failed outright.

Build the title in Java and strip surrounding whitespace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
