  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/a3be8defd648d8f0649b30379cbef999cf38fd60</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/jenkinsci/pipeline-input-step-plugin/commit/a3be8defd648d8f0649b30379cbef999cf38fd60"/>
    <title>
        Rely on jenkinsci organization release drafter configuration
    </title>
    <updated>2026-04-06T15:57:58Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156685?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>MarkEWaite</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/MarkEWaite</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Rely on jenkinsci organization release drafter configuration

Release drafter v7 dropped support for `_extends: .github` in the
configuration.  It either needs to be removed or replaced with a more
complete specification like:

`_extends: github:jenkinsci/.github:/.github/release-drafter.yml`

This pull request removes it because the &amp;quot;Enabling CD&amp;quot; instructions at
https://www.jenkins.io/doc/developer/publishing/releasing-cd/#configure-release-drafter
say:

&amp;gt; You can delete any existing Release Drafter configuration ... as that
&amp;gt; will be subsumed by the CD workflow

Testing done

* None.  Has worked well in many repositories, not expecting any issues in this repository&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
